['Name:\tpython', 'Umask:\t0022', 'State:\tR (running)', 'Tgid:\t3056', 'Ngid:\t0', 'Pid:\t3056', 'PPid:\t3054', 'TracerPid:\t0', 'Uid:\t1000\t1000\t1000\t1000', 'Gid:\t1000\t1000\t1000\t1000']

codex
The required preflight reached its Lean build step but exposed a sandbox/container defect: processes see namespace PIDs from `getpid()` while `/proc` is mounted with host PIDs, so Lean cannot resolve `/proc/<pid>/exe` and reports “failed to locate application.” This is infrastructure, not candidate evidence. I’m applying a narrow runtime shim in `/tmp/audit-work` that makes `getpid()` return the host PID parsed from `/proc/self/status`; I’ll rerun the same trusted `check_generation`, then run the mandated clean build under the same documented shim.
